# What ppcg has to report about this translation -- and what it must not.
#
# `rep` is never subscripted, so the caller's scop is right to say so
# once.  Saying it TWICE means the summary pass invented the annotation's
# arrays in a scop that mentions none of them.  The second claim is
# negated and spans the two reports, which a CMake regular expression
# does across newlines.
arena names never spelled in the source:.*rep
!never spelled in the source.*never spelled in the source
